<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA CREDIT EXPRESS BANK HAS ZERO 96 PROFIT.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA CREDIT EXPRESS BANK HAS ZERO 96 PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's private Credit Express</p>
<p>Bank posted zero net profit for 1996 compared to 32.4 million</p>
<p>levs net profit the year before, the bank's annual</p>
<p>profit-and-loss account published in the State Gazette showed.</p>
<p>Figures from the bank's balance sheet and profit-and-loss</p>
<p>account in million levs follow unless otherwise stated:</p>
<p>						     1996	    1995</p>
<p>Total revenue			     5,590.978	 389.356</p>
<p>Net income on financial</p>
<p>transactions				  625.363	 117.753</p>
<p>Business and administration costs     571.875	  46.513</p>
<p>Taxes					     7.249	  32.375</p>
<p>Profit						  0	  32.375</p>
<p>Provisions				     46.349	   0.540</p>
<p>Capital including</p>
<p>equity capital and provisions	   852.924	 832.915</p>
<p>Total assets				3,365.937	1,594.819</p>
<p>Financial assets			  2,171.344	  925.436</p>
<p>Attracted funds from financial</p>
<p>and non-financial clients	     2,277.075	  438.937</p>
<p>Items not included</p>
<p>in the balance *			  1,864.683	  138.738</p>
<p>* Under the Bulgarian accountancy standards items that are</p>
<p>not included in the balance involve guarantees issued by the</p>
<p>bank and other committments.</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 911 88</p>
</text>
